    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "manual",
      "slot": "(c) explanation",
      "desc": "Part (c): a correct answer says halving takes the same fraction of whatever is present, so each successive loss is smaller in absolute terms and the mass approaches zero without reaching it, whereas subtracting a fixed number of grams each period would remove the same amount every time and would drive the mass to zero and then below it, which is impossible. Full credit for contrasting a constant fraction with a constant amount and drawing the consequence; partial credit for naming the difference without the consequence.",
      "facet": "solve-with-the-model",
